<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Māori Language Act 1987</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1987</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Māori Language Act 1987 made te reo Māori an official language of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a> and gave the right to speak it in legal proceedings. It also created the Māori Language Commission to promote the language. Passed after a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/waitangi-tribunal">Waitangi Tribunal</a> finding that the language was a treasure protected by the Treaty of Waitangi, it was replaced by the Māori Language Act 2016.</p></div>
